experiments and rely less on third-party, remotely hosted solutions."},{"label":"Architecture","file":"arch.txt","command":"cat arch.txt","output":[{"text":"lan client","tone":"accent"}," |"," +-> :443  nginx (self-signed tls)"," |          |",{"text":"-+- docker -+--------------------------","tone":"dim"}," |          +-> auth     authentik --+"," |          +-> home     homarr      |"," |          +-> pihole   pihole      |"," |          +-> photos   immich -----+",{"text":" |          |            +- ml       |","tone":"dim"},{"text":" |          |            +- redis    |","tone":"dim"}," |          +-> docs     paperless --+"," |          +-> grafana  grafana     |",{"text":" |                       +- influxdb |","tone":"dim"}," |                       postgres <--+"," +-> :53   pihole -> upstream dns",{"text":"---------------------------------------","tone":"dim"},{"text":"# nginx forward-auth via authentik","tone":"dim"},{"text":"# lan only · no ports forwarded","tone":"dim"}],"prose":"Everything stays on the LAN. Pi-hole answers DNS for every device and filters queries before sending them upstream. NGINX terminates TLS with self-signed certs, checks sign-in with Authentik, and routes each .lan hostname to its container. Authentik, Immich, and Paperless-ngx share one Postgres instance, and Grafana charts metrics stored in InfluxDB."},{"label":"Stack","file":"deps","command":"cat deps","output":["+ Docker","+ NGINX","+ Fedora Linux",{"text":"3 dependencies","tone":"dim"}],"prose":"So as to not overcomplicate the system, these are the 3 core services that I use to host services, manage routing and DNS, and the core OS."}],"no":"04"}}],"$L12"]}],"$L13"],["$L14"],"$L15"]}],"p":"$@16","v":null,"s":"$a"}}]]
